# Trivy ignore list for the zonic-postgresql-server-fastapi runtime image.
#
# Every entry here is an OS-level package that ships with the python:3.12-slim
# (Debian 13 "trixie") base image and is not exercised by this application at
# runtime (no perl, no gzip/ncurses/sqlite3/acl usage anywhere in this codebase).
# Each CVE below currently has no upstream Debian fix available (or Debian has
# explicitly deferred one) as of the scan that first surfaced it, 2026-08-26 —
# `docker build` + `apt-get upgrade` alone cannot resolve these; they're pinned
# here rather than left to fail every build until Debian ships a patch.
#
# Re-check this list periodically (e.g. when bumping the base image) and remove
# entries once a real fix lands — don't let it become a permanent blanket waiver.

# gzip — buffer overflow in LZH decompression, no fix available
CVE-2026-41992

# libacl1 — symlink traversal privilege escalation, no fix available
CVE-2026-54369

# ncurses (libncursesw6, libtinfo6, ncurses-base, ncurses-bin) — buffer overflow,
# no fix available
CVE-2025-69720

# libsqlite3-0 — arbitrary code execution / crash via crafted FTS5 data, no fix
# available
CVE-2026-11822
CVE-2026-11824

# perl-base and its bundled CPAN modules — none of this is invoked by this
# service (no perl scripts, no Archive::Tar/IO::Compress/Storable usage)
CVE-2026-13221
CVE-2026-8376
CVE-2026-42496
CVE-2026-42497
CVE-2026-48962
CVE-2026-57432
CVE-2026-57433
CVE-2026-9538

# --- Added 2026-09-12 (build #50, 38 HIGH / 0 CRITICAL) ----------------------
#
# Five CVEs across util-linux and systemd, none with a Debian fix: every row in
# the trivy table had an empty "Fixed Version" column, and the Dockerfile
# already runs apt-get upgrade, so a rebuild cannot clear them.
#
# All five are LOCAL privilege escalation requiring the ability to execute the
# affected binary. This container runs as a non-root system user (uid 10001,
# see the Dockerfile) and the service spawns no processes at all -- no
# subprocess, no os.system, no shell-out anywhere in pgfoundation or
# pgfoundation_api. Nothing in the request path can reach mount(8), nsenter(8)
# or systemd-homed.
#
# util-linux (bsdutils, libblkid1, liblastlog2-2, libmount1, libsmartcols1,
# libuuid1, login, mount, util-linux) -- mount-helper, nsenter --join-cgroup
# and bind-mount handling. This service mounts nothing; the only "mount" in
# the codebase is FastAPI router mounting.
CVE-2026-76642
CVE-2026-78408
CVE-2026-78409
CVE-2026-78410

# libsystemd0 -- systemd-homed local privilege escalation. systemd-homed is not
# installed or running in this image; libsystemd0 is present only as a
# transitive dependency of the base image's package set.
CVE-2026-16742
